MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What I was thinking of was processing where the raw data in HDFS is a mess -- awkward format, missing fields and lots of stuff I don't need to include for my computation. In Hadoop Streaming the first job of the mapper script will be to filter this down to something usable by the reducer. In plain R, too, I often have this situation and I'd rather not use R's string processing and regex functions, because pipe() is much simpler. It means I can push the parsing work outside of R, so all R sees is a clean n-column feed.

From u6ac7e7dfbe4f6c38 at groups.google.com  Fri Jun  7 07:39:37 2013
From: u6ac7e7dfbe4f6c38 at groups.google.com (Antonio Piccolboni)
