From: u63023c771a070260 at groups.google.com (Antonio Piccolboni)
Date: Thu, 20 Jun 2013 16:56:00 +0000
Subject: rmr 2.2.1 released
Message-ID: <E2EK8Nydo5o.LnqLMiQnsxUJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/E2EK8Nydo5o/m/LnqLMiQnsxUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The most important piece of news is compatibility with windows (you need HDP 1.1 for windows for this to work, at least this is the combination that passed testing), plus bug fixes and minor speed improvements. Details here <https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/rmr2/blob/2.2.1/docs/new-in-this-release.md>.

Antonio

From u63023c771a070260 at groups.google.com  Fri Jun 21 22:41:52 2013
From: u63023c771a070260 at groups.google.com (Antonio Piccolboni)
Date: Fri, 21 Jun 2013 22:41:52 +0000
Subject: rhbase 1.2.0 and rhdfs 1.0.6 released
Message-ID: <XRFY8XyXTK0.4ybRqOts-YcJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/XRFY8XyXTK0/m/4ybRqOts-YcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rhdfs adds windows compatibility (when used with HDP for windows). rhbase has a new serialization option, "character", which is appropriate when cell contents are textual. This was previously and not so accurately named "raw". "raw" is now really raw, meaning cell contents are represented with raw vectors, no transformation occurs.

Antonio

